# Files excluded from the deployment (not from git). Same syntax as
# .gitignore — anything matched here is never uploaded, so it 404s rather
# than being served.
#
# A game folder holds its dev source next to its shipped builds (see
# games/README.md). Only the version folders are the deliverable; the source
# beside them has no business being fetchable. Patterned on games/*/ rather
# than named after one game, so every future game folder inherits it.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: games/*/v1/ and any later version folder — those
# are the playable builds the site serves.
games/*/src/
games/*/build.mjs
games/*/package.json
games/*/_reference/
games/*/BUILD.md
games/*/CLAUDE.md
games/*/README.md
# The Photon SDK is dev-side too: the built game resolves it relative to
# itself (games/<name>/v1/public/...), so this copy was never the one a
# shipped build would load. If multiplayer is ever switched on, build.mjs
# has to place it inside the version folder — not un-ignore it here.
games/*/public/

# Anything parked for possible reuse: songs swapped out of Top Picks, retired
# artwork, and so on. Kept in the repo, never shipped — there is no reason to
# upload assets the site does not reference. One rule rather than one per
# folder, matching the leading-underscore convention bake_images.py skips.
**/_archive/
